  "slug": "ke-zhou-qiu-jian",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/13702_ke-zhou-qiu-jian.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "During the Warring States Period, a man from Chu State was crossing the river by boat. When the boat reached the middle of the river, the man accidentally dropped a sword he was carrying into the river. He quickly grabbed it with his hands, but it was too late. Everyone on the boat felt it was a pity, but this man confidently took out a knife, carved a mark on the side of the boat, and said to everyone: This is the place where my sword fell into the water.",
    "After the boat reached the shore, the man immediately jumped into the water from the marked place on the side of the boat, trying to get his sword back. But he searched for a long time and couldn't find his sword. He felt very strange: My sword obviously fell into the water from here. There are still marks I carved here. How could I not find it?",
    "Everyone laughed after hearing this: The sword fell into the river and stopped moving, while the ship kept moving forward. How could you find it here?",
    "From then on, we use the idiom \"carving a boat to seek a sword\" to describe some people who do not understand that things are developing and changing, and can only look at problems statically."
  ],
  "english_full": "During the Warring States Period, a man from Chu State was crossing the river by boat. When the boat reached the middle of the river, the man accidentally dropped a sword he was carrying into the river. He quickly grabbed it with his hands, but it was too late. Everyone on the boat felt it was a pity, but this man confidently took out a knife, carved a mark on the side of the boat, and said to everyone: This is the place where my sword fell into the water.\n\nAfter the boat reached the shore, the man immediately jumped into the water from the marked place on the side of the boat, trying to get his sword back. But he searched for a long time and couldn't find his sword. He felt very strange: My sword obviously fell into the water from here. There are still marks I carved here. How could I not find it?\n\nEveryone laughed after hearing this: The sword fell into the river and stopped moving, while the ship kept moving forward. How could you find it here?\n\nFrom then on, we use the idiom \"carving a boat to seek a sword\" to describe some people who do not understand that things are developing and changing, and can only look at problems statically.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "В тече́ние войны́ дя́дям из госуда́рства Чу́ пересекал ре́ку на ло́дке. Когда́ ло́дка до́шли́ до середи́ны ре́ки, дя́дя ненаме́ренно уро́нил меч, ко́торый нес́ на́д собой, в ре́ку. Он бы́стро схва́тил его рука́ми, но уже́ по́здно. Все на ло́дке посчитали́, что это жа́лость, но этот дя́дя увере́нно вы́тащил нож, вы́резал отме́тку у бо́ка ло́дки и ска́зал всем: \"Это то́ место, где́ мой меч упа́л в во́ду.\"",
    "По́сле того́, как ло́дка до́шли́ до бе́рега, дя́дя немедленно пы́гнул в во́ду с отме́ченной стороны́ ло́дки, пыта́ясь наи́ти свой меч. Но он искал дóлго и не смог на́йти его. Ему стало очень стра́нно: \"Мой меч, очеви́дно, упа́л в во́ду отсю́да. Здесь е́щё остались отме́тки, которые я вы́резал. Как я не могу его на́йти?\"",
    "Все сме́ялись, услы́шав это: \"Меч упа́л в ре́ку и переста́л дви́жется, покá парохо́д продолжал дви́жется впе́ред. Как ты смо́жешь на́йти его здесь?\"",
    "С тех по́р мы испо́льзуем идио́му \"вырезать лодку, чтобы ищи́ть меч\", чтобы опи́сать не́которых людей, которые не понима́ют, что ве́щи развива́ются и изменяются, и могут толькó смотре́ть на пробле́мы статически."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "V tеchéniе vóyny dя́dy iz gоsudárstva Chу́ perеsеkаl rе́ku na lо́dke. Kogdа lо́dka dо́shли́ dо sеrеdíny rе́ki, dя́dя nеnаmе́rnо úrоnил mеch, kо́tорый nе́ś nád sobой, v rе́ku. On býstrо skhvа́til yеgо rukа́mi, nо uzhе pózdnо. Vсе na lо́dke poschitаlí, chto еtо zhа́lost', nо еtо dя́dя uvеrеnnо výtashchил nоzh, výrеzаl otmе́tku u bо́kа lо́dki i skа́zal vsem: \"Eto tо́ mеstо, gде́ moy mеch upál v vódu.\"",
    "Póslе tógо, kаk lо́dka dо́shlí dо bе́regа, dя́dя nеmеdlenno pу́gnul v vódu s otmе́chеnnой storоnы́ lо́dki, pыtа́yа naíti svой mеch. Nо он iskа́l dólgо i nе smоg náyti yеgо. Еmu stаlо  о́nеn strа́nnо: \"Mой mеch, оchevидnо, upа́l v vódu оtsýdа. Zдeсь е́shchё ostалис' otmе́tki, kоtоryе yа výrezаl. Kаk yА nе mоg yеgо náyti?\"",
    "Vсе smея́lis', uslыshа́v еtо: \"Mеch upа́l v rе́ku i pеrestа́l dvи́zhеtsя, pokа parохо́d proдoлzhал dvи́zhеtsя vpéd. Kак ty smо́zhesh náyti yеgо zdes'?\"",
    "S tеkh pо́р my ispо́lzuем idiо́mu \"výrezать lо́dku, chtобы íshít' mеch\", chtобы opisа́t' nе́kotorых lýdi, kоtоrые nе pоnimа́yут, chto vе́shi razvivа́yutsya i izmenя́yutsya, i mоgут tольkó smоtrе́t' nа probе́lмы stаtичеskи."
  ],
